Z||000024||GTFiero1||12-02-2001||02:05 AM||||wait wait wait...he built it himself and he built the engine himself right? he said its 4 stroke right? does this mean he makes his own spark plugs???? he cant use glow plugs from the 2 strokes that are in remote controlled cars and planes and such. So where would he get the spark plugs from? ||||reg||1
Z||000025||California Kid||12-02-2001||02:42 AM||||There are actual spark plugs that small, they are used in 4 cycle model aircraft engines.  Master Machinist are really cool, they can make anything! Just imagine doing the camshaft / distributor / and crank for a V12 in miniature!!<P>Had a neighbor (Master Mach) that used to make working models of 16 cylinder 4 cycle radial aircraft engines, they were about 6 inches in diameter. He also made a steam locomotive (last model before they changed to fuel), it was about 3 ft long, and had everything right down to ultra small pressure gauge. If you took pictures of these pieces you couldn't tell them from the real thing.<p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||88-DOHC||12-02-2001||02:43 AM||||There is such things as small scale 4 stroke engines. The same kind of engine you find in your average gas powered remote controled car, but its 4 stroke.  For that matter there is even small scale wankel engines that are about the size of your hand for RC applications.  Exactly how the 4 stroke versions generate their spark I am not sure. However I can say, that what they use does look very similar to a glow plug (but it is different). From the video the car looked roughly equivalent to 1/5 scale RC models. In any case, if worse came to worse, he could have made (or had made) his own tiny spark plugs. I wouldn't put it past him seeing how much trouble he went to making everything else.<p>[This message has been edited by 88-DOHC (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||Nashco||12-02-2001||02:58 AM||||THAT IS AMAZING!!!  Think of all the intricate parts...engine management stuff in particular (spark and fuel controllers)!!  So much detail..INCREDIBLE!!!<P>This guy will no doubt be getting lots of publicity throughout the car world as word travels.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
